  "term": "AChE",
  "definition": "AChE, or acetylcholinesterase, is an enzyme made from the human ACHE gene. It helps break down acetylcholine and is also involved in neuronal apoptosis and in the structure of the Cartwright (Yt) blood group antigen.",
